{
 "notes": "size_class fish on every row (added by Claude Code with the §EK hunt, 5 Oct): what a camp brings back from a fishing trip. Fish and sea creatures in the creatures.json schema plus D4 fields; spawn disabled until Phase 7. Each carries `needs.water_kind` (river/lake/sea), `salt`, `depth_m`, and a `habitat` label; species appear only in their water — river fish never in the sea, reef fish never in cold water — so every biome's water has its own fish. `school.size` > 1 means shoals rendered as one instanced body of many fish. `bait` lists what each takes, and the bait table says where each bait comes from: the fishing loop reads both, so worms catch trout and only a flying fish that landed in your boat at night catches a marlin. Sharks, orcas and the wels are apex_water and hunt the schools; `scent_drawn` species come to blood and carcasses in the water; `hazard` species can hurt a wading or swimming player; `landmark` creatures (whales, whale shark, manta, giant squid) are rare boat encounters the lore system may name; whales `migration` pole-to-tropic with the seasons, and the humpback's song is audible through a boat hull at night. Flying fish glide and land in boats. Salmon run upstream in autumn (reads flow_to) and leap the waterfalls.",
 "bait": {
  "worm": "dug from soil with hands or shovel; universal freshwater bait",
  "insect": "caught from foliage or a snag; trout, grayling, tilapia",
  "fly": "a feather lure tied from a bird feather and cord; trout, salmon, mahseer",
  "minnow": "a small fish used live; pike, bass, barracuda",
  "frog": "caught at a pond; bass, pike, snakehead",
  "fish_scrap": "cut from a caught fish; catfish, cod, sharks",
  "meat": "a piece of any carcass; catfish, piranha, sharks — and it draws them",
  "bread": "camp bread; carp, tilapia",
  "berry": "foraged; carp and mahseer near overhanging bushes",
  "fruit": "a fallen fig; mahseer",
  "salmon_egg": "from a spawning salmon; trout",
  "squid": "caught at night by lantern light from a boat; tuna, swordfish, grouper",
  "crab": "from rocky shore or mangrove; sea bass, grouper",
  "feather": "a bare feather lure; mackerel",
  "flying_fish": "one that landed in the boat at night; marlin, sailfish, mahi-mahi, tuna",
  "seal": "a seal carcass; great white only"
 },
